      "result": {
        "reply_text": "I understand that you paid for a washing machine repair service in Kanpur, but the machine still leaks and the company is not responding to you. You have your service bill and videos as proof.\n\nUnder the law, a product service provider is liable if the service they provided was faulty, deficient, or did not follow the terms of your contract. You may bring a product liability action against them for the harm caused by this deficient service.\n\nYou can first try to register your grievance through the National Consumer Helpline (NCH). This is a pre-litigation step. You can contact them by calling 1915, using the NCH app, visiting their website (consumerhelpline.gov.in), or sending an email to nch-ca@gov.in.\n\nIf the issue is not resolved, you may file a formal complaint with the District Commission. The District Commission has the power to hear complaints where the value of the service paid does not exceed fifty lakh rupees. You can file this complaint in the district where the service provider carries on business or where the cause of action arose.\n\nKeep your service bill and the videos of the leak safe, as these are your evidence. You must file your complaint within two years from the date the problem occurred.\n\nPlease provide the name of the repair service company and the specific date in October 2026 when the repair took place.\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 82\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 85\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 34\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\nSource: Consumer Protection (Jurisdiction of the District Commission, the State Commission and the National Commission) Rules, 2021, rule 3\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- The specific procedure for filing a complaint electronically beyond the NCH portal.\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
